Compare the two blind cleaned documents using the V0.6.2.1 order.

First classify each side as substantive main content, non-main-only, or
unreadable. Then run the conflict veto before rewarding overlap: a different
title, SKU, record/volume/chapter/page/image ID, site/domain/brand/controller,
date, price, list member, state, or page role requires no/no even inside an
otherwise identical template. Cookie, legal, auth, error, paywall, navigation,
and shared-template text cannot be the substantive anchor.

Use near_surface only after establishing the same substantive record or the
same complete non-main-only message with no identity/role conflict. Use
containment only when there is a non-empty shared page-specific anchor and one
side adds meaningful main content without any conflicting slot. A short
substantive anchor can prove real containment; a generic footer cannot.

Before returning, reconcile relation, both directions, and materiality. Every
resolved non-exact result needs separately labeled A and B quoted literal spans
copied from the corresponding documents, at most 240 characters each, without
ellipses. For no/no quote the conflicting value/role on both sides; for a
duplicate quote the shared substantive anchor on both sides. If exact bilateral
evidence is unavailable, return the fully unresolved/low result. Truncated
input can never receive high confidence.

